3000
03:13:46,860 --> 03:13:48,880
I actually knew a guy from Finland named Heiko.

3001
03:13:51,200 --> 03:13:54,260
It's spelled the same way as 2Ks.

3002
03:14:00,250 --> 03:14:01,590
What's happening down here?

3003
03:14:06,080 --> 03:14:07,000
Nothing exciting.

3004
03:14:09,800 --> 03:14:11,020
Now that's exciting.

3005
03:14:17,490 --> 03:14:18,310
Grant me access.

3006
03:14:22,390 --> 03:14:24,950
Also, did I change the death counter here?

3007
03:14:27,330 --> 03:14:28,530
I think I did.

3008
03:14:30,590 --> 03:14:31,150
Cool.

3009
03:14:32,970 --> 03:14:34,490
We're at 73 deaths.

3010
03:14:35,730 --> 03:14:36,830
I've had them, not today, actually.

3011
03:14:38,470 --> 03:14:40,290
I'm not having very successful runs here.

3012
03:14:41,130 --> 03:14:42,990
That last death was really bad, though.

3013
03:14:45,190 --> 03:14:47,150
I completely fucked that one up.

3014
03:14:51,040 --> 03:14:52,360
I panicked a little bit.

3015
03:14:55,520 --> 03:15:00,620
It's much easier to get into those situations where you panic when you don't have a good want.

3016
03:15:00,980 --> 03:15:06,360
Because you shoot at an enemy, you don't kill him, which gives the enemy another opportunity to shoot you.

3017
03:15:07,140 --> 03:15:10,600
But then you shoot again, and you still don't kill him, which gives the enemy another opportunity to shoot you.

3018
03:15:10,680 --> 03:15:15,160
And in the meantime, you've spent all this time trying to kill him, another enemy shows up, and it all snowballs from there.

3019
03:15:15,820 --> 03:15:19,720
In other words, everything goes bad when you don't have a good want.

3020
03:15:19,960 --> 03:15:22,100
I mean, it's kind of obvious when you say it.

3021
03:15:23,800 --> 03:15:27,720
There's so many factors going into what happens when you have a shit want, you know?

3022
03:15:27,780 --> 03:15:28,540
That makes it even worse.

